API & Web Application Security Testing
Overview

This repository provides a practical framework for testing the security of web applications and APIs, with a primary focus on authentication, authorization, access control, and common web security vulnerabilities.

The project documents security testing methodologies, test cases, sample HTTP requests, vulnerability assessment procedures, and remediation recommendations for authorized security assessments.

Objectives
Identify authentication and authorization weaknesses.
Test for Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA) and IDOR.
Evaluate Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
Validate JWT and session management security.
Assess REST API endpoints and HTTP methods.
Identify common web application vulnerabilities.
Document security findings with reproducible steps.
Recommend secure implementation and remediation practices.
Scope of Testing
1. Authentication Testing
Login and logout functionality
Password reset and account recovery
Multi-factor authentication
Session expiration and invalidation
JWT signature and claim validation
2. Authorization Testing
Horizontal privilege escalation
Vertical privilege escalation
Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR)
Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA)
Broken Function Level Authorization (BFLA)
Role and permission enforcement
Multi-tenant data isolation
3. API Security Testing
REST API endpoint authorization
HTTP method restrictions
Input validation
Mass assignment
Excessive data exposure
Rate limiting and resource consumption
CORS and security configuration
4. Web Application Security
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
SQL Injection
Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)
File upload validation
Security misconfiguration
Security header validation
Testing Methodology
Define the authorized scope and testing objectives.
Identify application endpoints and user roles.
Establish baseline behavior using legitimate accounts.
Test access controls with different user identities.
Validate expected and actual responses.
Document reproducible findings and supporting evidence.
Assess impact and assign severity.
Recommend remediation and perform retesting.
